# allocrefused.tcyr -- 2.2.0, ADR-0008. A refused allocation is reported as
# PRANI_ERR_ALLOC, by every prani constructor and entry point, for every
# allocation prani makes.
#
# Through 2.1.2 prani called `alloc`, `vec_new` and `vec_push` directly. A refused
# `alloc` returned 0 and prani stored through it (a fault at the null page); a
# refused `vec_new` returned 0 and prani used it as a vec; a refused `vec_push` grow
# exited the process ("vec: alloc failed"). Since 2.2.0 every allocation goes
# through src/error.cyr's funnel (prani_alloc / prani_vec_new / prani_vec_push),
# whose memory comes from prani_alloc_raw, and scripts/check-alloc.sh fails the
# build if src/ allocates any other way.
#
# THE MECHANISM. cycc keeps the last definition of a function, so this suite
# redefines two:
#   prani_alloc_raw  -- prani's allocator. Refusing here refuses prani's requests
#                       and nobody else's: svara's own allocations do not pass
#                       through it, and stop at the null page when refused
#                       (svara ADR-0009), which would end the run, not fail it.
#   alloc            -- the stdlib's, as svara's and naad's suites replace it: a
#                       bump arena on one private mapping. Refusing HERE reaches
#                       naad's constructors, which report a refusal (naad
#                       ADR-0010), and the two places prani passes that on.
# While armed each counts requests and refuses one:
#   FI_ONE   the Nth request only
#   FI_FROM  the Nth request and every later one (a heap that stays exhausted)
#
# Every count is measured here, not written down, so a toolchain or dependency
# that allocates differently moves the indices, not the expectations. Every sweep
# has a floor, so it cannot pass by refusing nothing, and a control refuses one
# past the last request and requires the unrefused result, bit for bit.
#
# ⚠ This build warns twice, on purpose:
#   duplicate fn 'prani_alloc_raw' / 'alloc' (last definition wins)
# The overrides are the mechanism. svara's and naad's suites carry the same.

